<div class="dmarc-view" data-dmarc-root>
  <div class="card">
    <h2>DMARC reports <span class="hint">aggregate (rua) feedback from receiving mail providers</span></h2>

    <%# Ingest health comes FIRST and deliberately. An empty summary because
        nothing has fetched in a week looks identical to "no problems", which
        is the worst possible failure mode for a compliance view -- so the
        freshness of the data is stated before the data. %>
    <div id="dmarc-status" class="dmarc-status"><p class="muted">Loading…</p></div>

    <div class="field" style="max-width:16rem;">
      <label for="dmarc-days">Window</label>
      <select id="dmarc-days">
        <option value="7">last 7 days</option>
        <option value="30" selected>last 30 days</option>
        <option value="90">last 90 days</option>
        <option value="365">last year</option>
      </select>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>By domain <span class="hint">is any of our own mail failing alignment?</span></h2>
    <div class="scrollbox">
      <table class="dmarc-table">
        <thead><tr>
          <th>Domain</th><th>Policy</th><th class="num">Messages</th>
          <th class="num">Aligned</th><th class="num">Failing</th>
          <th class="num">Quarantined<br>/rejected</th>
          <th class="num">Reporters</th><th class="num">Sources</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody id="dmarc-summary-body"><tr><td colspan="8" class="muted">Loading…</td></tr></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="font-size:0.8rem;margin:0.5rem 0 0;">
      “Aligned” and “Failing” are DMARC’s own evaluation — a message can carry a
      valid DKIM signature and still fail if the signing domain doesn’t align
      with the From header.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>By sending source <span class="hint">who is sending mail as us</span></h2>
    <label class="dmarc-inline"><input type="checkbox" id="dmarc-only-failing" checked> only sources with failures</label>
    <div class="scrollbox">
      <table class="dmarc-table">
        <thead><tr>
          <th>Source IP</th><th>Domain</th><th class="num">Messages</th>
          <th class="num">Aligned</th><th class="num">Failing</th>
          <th class="num">Reporters</th><th>Last seen</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody id="dmarc-sources-body"><tr><td colspan="7" class="muted">Loading…</td></tr></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="font-size:0.8rem;margin:0.5rem 0 0;">
      A source that isn’t ours, sending volume that fails, is the signal to
      look at before moving any domain from <code>quarantine</code> to
      <code>reject</code>. Our own senders should appear here with everything
      aligned.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Reports received</h2>
    <div class="scrollbox">
      <table class="dmarc-table">
        <thead><tr>
          <th>Reporter</th><th>Domain</th><th>Window</th>
          <th class="num">Messages</th><th class="num">Records</th><th>Ingested</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody id="dmarc-reports-body"><tr><td colspan="6" class="muted">Loading…</td></tr></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
